const tips={tourButton:'Play or resume the continuous two-minute Solar flight. Exit, Esc or any flight action hands manual control back at the current scene.',helpButton:'All controls, numerical checks and model limits (?)',physics:'Equations, published comparisons and renderer verification',bridge:'Glide to the center of the bubble, keeping your current viewing direction (V)',external:'Glides out facing the bridge look direction, from behind the ship. Drag orbits; Shift/right-drag pans. Ship, planets and sky use the same delayed-light model in Optical view (V).',speedExact:'Precise speed in c; for example 0.0001 c is about 30 km/s. Applies immediately. The main slider remains a coarse cruise control.',velocity:'Snapshot speed, 0–50 c; applies immediately. With assist it is a speed limit. Pause holds time while preserving this optical snapshot.',warpToggle:'F switches delayed-light optics and the current-position layout. Flight speed and position stay the same.',cameraButton:'Field of view and external camera distance',orbitTarget:'Move only the outside camera near the selected current target. The ship continues flying.',dragMode:'Cycle left-drag Orbit, Pan or Look; the Pan mode also works on touch screens. Shift/right-drag pans in the screen plane. IJKL looks; Shift+IJKL orbits. Wheel zooms; Y restores bubble framing.',cameraFocus:'Choose a following, target-orbiting or released outside observer.',mapScale:'Fixed coordinate map scale; it does not change with speed.',overlayCycle:'G opens the current-position layout, then cycles its shell / diagnostic paths / off. F returns to optics.',pause:'Hold simulation time to inspect a snapshot. The speed setting still defines its optics. Camera remains available (Space).',reset:'Reset flight, heading, camera and visits (R)',quality:'Adaptive adjusts angular and pixel budgets for smooth flight. High uses native pixel detail; Low lowers resolution. Pause to refine the numerical map.',clean:'Hide interface (H). Press H again or Show controls to restore.',backend:'Auto prefers WebGPU. WebGL 2 is the fallback; the browser selects Metal/GPU.',sceneMode:'Deep survey or a Solar System with common size/distance scale, prescribed orbits and retarded optical surfaces.',destinationSelect:'Choose the highlighted navigation target. N cycles targets.',lookTarget:'O aims the current camera toward the target navigation position without steering or moving the ship. The optical image may be displaced.',nextDestination:'Highlight the next checkpoint or planet (N)',assistMode:'Approach holds near the planet. Flyby plans an offset pass outside the curved bubble region, then releases at your actual speed/heading. Starting too close first triggers a slow clearance move.',courseAssist:'P steers toward the selected target, slows while turning and approaches it. Solar Approach holds at a standoff; Flyby passes and releases. Disengaging or steering manually keeps the actual speed, not the former limit.',exploreToggle:'Toggle HUD direction arrows, current-position target highlights and map guides. Flight assist and optical bodies are unaffected.',inspectTarget:'Reposition the ship near this planet, set speed to zero and pause. This is an explicit visit, not a simulated flight.',centerView:'C looks at the current focus (outside) or along the ship heading (bridge). It does not move the observer. Optical images can be displaced from that current direction.',resetHeading:'X resets ship heading without moving the observer. Z also recenters look.',sky:'Choose the artistic distant sky (B)',benchmark:'Measure ten seconds of submitted-frame intervals (T)',frameBubble:'Y frames the bubble facing the bridge look direction, including up/down. Distance follows warp speed so the bending region stays visible. Drag orbits; Shift/right-drag pans; wheel takes over zoom.',wideRear:'Y aligns with the bridge look direction and frames the bubble with speed-aware distance and an 80° field of view.',cameraReset:'Align with bridge look and restore speed-aware bubble framing and an 80° field of view',exposureToggle:'Display assistance meters center exposure and adds gentle surface fill so night-side planet textures remain readable. Off restores stronger day/night contrast. Colors and surface lighting are illustrative; frequency gain remains bolometric.'};
